public boolImagick::quantizeImages intnumberColors intcolorspace inttreedepth booldither boolmeasureError
Reduces the number of unique colors in all the images of the sequence to at most numberColors. Unlike Imagick::quantizeImage, which only processes the current image, the colors of all the images are analyzed together to choose a single set of colors which best represents the whole sequence, and the pixels of every image are then mapped to the colors of that set. This is useful, for example, to produce frames sharing a common palette for an animated GIF.
